  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved socio-economic status of women, youths, marginalized groups in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ireland Civil Society Programme (ICSP) project, is a five years (2023 to 2027) multi -country project that will be implemented in Zambia, Malawi and Zimbabwe. In Zambia the targeted districts are Mongu, Gwembe, Kaoma and Namwala and will incorporate the nexus programming approach for the Gender Justice, Humanitarian and Agriculture and Food Systems themes. The programme is aimed at improving the socio -economic status of women, the youth and marginalized groups such as those living with disabilities will change the lives of the target groups in three key result areas. Firstly, through this programme diverse women, girls and marginalized groups will be supported to fully realize their socio -economic rights, exercise their leadership and live a life free from violence, discrimination and poverty.</narrative>
  </description>
